    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.icons\n\n### Description\n\nI'm using Kitty terminal and have a nerd font `ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd 3.3.0-1`, I can't get the icon to be displayed in the overflow view...\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.0-dev-1226+gaf112e605d\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `:=MiniIcons.get('file','file.lua')`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nShould display the icon with the overflow view.",
