            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This doesn't look like an issue with 'mini.icons' per se.\r\n\r\nHere are the steps that might help here:\r\n- Install different font or [use suggested fallback](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ccfc6300a5c17387f2899f979ecc04f942bee2a0/doc/mini-icons.txt#L61-L63). Probably try the pakcage without 'mono' in the title as some fonts might have that to indicate that *all* its glyphs should be rendered in a single cell.\r\n- Try following [this recommendation](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/faq/#kitty-is-not-able-to-use-my-favorite-font) and adjust [`symbol_map`](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.symbol_map).\r\n- Check that [`narrow_symbols`](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.narrow_symbols) option does not override default \"overflow\" logic.",
